          %title
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong non-unital operad
            is a structure like an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            but without a unit or operadic identity. However, in contrast to operads where the multiplication operation substitutes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            operations simultaneously into a single
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
          %p
            It is possible to package these individual substitution operations into a single operation, using not the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plethysm"} plethystic
            or substitution monoidal product (usually denoted
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
            = succeed "." do
              %em graft product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            equipped with an associative product
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ F \to F
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p There are various possible notions of non-unital operad; here we focus on the permutative and non-permutative cases.
          %h3#graft_product_of_permutative_species Graft product of (permutative) species
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FB
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FB
            be the monoidal groupoid of finite sets and bijections, where the monoidal product is obtained by restricting the coproduct on the category of finite sets. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo :
                  %mi FB
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F, G: FB \to V
            be (Joyal) species valued in a bicomplete symmetric monoidal closed category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %strong graft product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo *
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \ast G
            is defined by the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo *
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi S
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \ast G)[S] = \sum_{T \subseteq S} F[S/T] \otimes G[T]
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/T
            denotes the pushout of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \to 1
            along the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subseteq S
            in the category of finite sets. This includes the degenerate case where
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/0
            is the result of freely adjoining a point to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi F
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \mapsto F'
            defined by the formula
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F'[S] = F[S/0]
          %p
            The set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/T
            has
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T/T
            as distinguished basepoint, and if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is complementary to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi U
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/T \cong U + \{T/T\} \cong U/0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mo *
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi U
                              %mo +
                              %mi T
                              %mo =
                              %mi S
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo +
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi U
                              %mo +
                              %mi T
                              %mo =
                              %mi S
                          %mi F
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (F \ast G)[S] &amp; \cong &amp; \sum_{U + T = S} F[U + *] \otimes G[T] \\
                  \&amp; \cong &amp; \sum_{U + T = S} F'[U] \otimes G[T] \\
                  \&amp; \cong &amp; (F' \otimes G)[S]
                  }
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            refers to the usual Day convolution product on species, induced from the tensor product on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FB
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FB
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi FB
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo +
                      %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi FB
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{FB} \stackrel{- + *}{\to} V^{FB},
          %p is cocontinuous, and since Day convolution is cocontinuous in each of its arguments, we see that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
